{"role":"assistant","content":"Done. All six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` are implemented via the existing `Analytics.capture` wrapper, and the write-up is in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Registration screen** (`lib/screens/registration_screen.dart`)\n- `registration_email_started` / `registration_phone_started` — fire once, the first time each field goes from empty to typed-in (`onChanged`).\n- `loan_amount_changed` — fires from the slider's `onChangeEnd` with `{'amount': v.round()}` (int), i.e. once per adjustment with the chosen amount, not per drag tick.\n- `terms_accepted` — fires only when the checkbox is ticked (unticking sends nothing).\n- `registration_continue_tapped` — fires on Continue before navigation, with `amount` (int) and `terms` (bool).\n\n**Offers screen** (`lib/screens/offer_screen.dart`)\n- Converted to a `StatefulWidget` with a `ScrollController`. A listener fires `offers_scrolled` with `{'offset': offset}` (double, pixels) whenever the scroll position has moved ≥50 px since the last event — guarantees the funnel event fires without per-pixel flooding.\n\nNo email/phone values are sent, and no screen-view events were added (already covered by `PosthogObserver`).\n\nOne caveat: `flutter analyze` couldn't run here — macOS blocks this shell from executing the Flutter SDK, and dependencies were never resolved. I verified instead by type-checking the actual sources with the Dart 3.11.5 analyzer against API-faithful stubs of `flutter`/`posthog_flutter` in a temp dir (removed afterwards): no issues found. Worth a real `flutter analyze` wherever the SDK is accessible."}
